summary: The questions the watcher left open, now settled: a per-repository choice of source given up.

* ''A per-repository choice of source: given up'' (user, 27 November 2026). Forcing inotify for one repository while the broker serves the others was never asked for; the socket stays the only switch. The case it would serve, a part of a tree the broker does not see, is already handled on its own: a mount the broker does not cover is watched by an inotify source scoped to it ([[Uncovered mounts]]).
